course: dictionary
lesson: 12525
title: Desirable: worth wanting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Desirable is an adjective. It describes something that people want or think is good. «The new bike was desirable, with bright lights and a fast gear.» The bike is worth wanting, so desirable means something good that you would like to have.
explain: Look at the word parts: desire means wanting, and -able means can be. So desirable means able to be wanted. Something desirable is useful, attractive or good, like a desirable house with a big garden.
explain: Desirable can also be a formal word for a good idea. «Experience is desirable but not essential for this job.» Here it means experience helps and is a good idea, but you do not have to have it. Always check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Desirable means worth having or wanting.
fact: Desirable can mean good, useful or attractive.
fact: In formal writing, desirable can mean advisable, which means a good idea.
fact: «A desirable outcome of the test is that everyone passes.» Here, desirable means a good result.
fact: The opposite of desirable is undesirable, which means not wanted or not good.
exercise: «The school library has a desirable collection of books.» What does desirable mean here? | *Worth having and good to use | Very cheap | Hard to read | Far away
exercise: «Experience is desirable but not essential for this job.» What does desirable mean here? | *It helps and is a good idea, but it is not required | It is forbidden | It is the same as essential | It must be done at once
exercise: Find and copy the word that means not wanted or not good. | fine | desirable | pleasant | *undesirable
test: Maya says desirable means shiny. What is the best meaning? | *Attractive, good or worth having | Shiny like metal | Noisy | Cheap and old
test: «A desirable outcome of the experiment is clean water for everyone.» What is a desirable outcome? | A result nobody counts | *A good result that people want | Something bad that happens | A random accident
exam: Jayden reads «The house was desirable, so many people wanted to buy it.» What does desirable suggest? | *Worth wanting and attractive to buyers | Dirty and broken | Very far from the town | Too small to live in
